# Game page implementation structure

Site is in **development stage**. Do **not** add SEO alias redirects unless explicitly requested.

Every new / updated game page follows the Home + Daily Challenge + Minecraft pattern:

## Page shell (`app/.../page.tsx`)

1. `Header` + `main` + `Footer`
2. Playable game component first (above the fold)
3. SEO article component below the game
4. Metadata: title, description, keywords, canonical
5. FAQ JSON-LD when the article exports FAQ items

## Game component

- Mode chrome as needed (Daily / Unlimited / themed)
- Real playable dive (prompts, timer, submit/pass, reveal, results)
- Music/SFX via existing dive audio patterns; mute only stops audio

## SEO article component

- Human-tone guide (not thin keyword stuffing)
- Sections: what it is → how to play → scoring/tiers → tips → FAQ → related games
- Cross-links to Daily Dive, Unlimited, other modes, home guide
- Fan-made / trademark disclaimer when the theme needs it (e.g. Minecraft)

## Screenshots (required)

Use `ArticleShot` with **real gameplay** images under `public/screenshots/` — not lobby-only or marketing UI alone.

Capture at least:

1. **Prompt** — question + timer + answer field + Pass/Submit
2. **Reveal** — valid rare hit (tier + points + depth)
3. **Miss** — nothing landed / timeout / pass + continue
4. **Results** — dive complete / score / depth / rundown

Capture rules:

- Prefer full viewport screenshots of the game in play (prompt through results)
- Avoid clipped HUD-only strips
- Wire shots into the article next to the matching section
- Cache-bust with `?v=N` when replacing images

## Do not

- Ship a game page with article text but no gameplay screenshots
- Reuse the same non-gameplay image for every section
- Add redirect aliases (`/krillion-unlimited`, typo routes, etc.) until asked
- Hide unfinished features behind “coming soon” when the brief says to build them
